          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "chaojun-zhang"
            },
            "body": "Without an out-of-place copy, this causes an all-zero-accuracy issue under torch.compile — see https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/39844.\r\n\r\nIf we really want to use inplace allreduce, we may need to rely on an environment variable or some other mechanism to determine whether inplace is actually safe to use here. torch.compiler.is_compiling() doesn't work when use custom op all_reduce.",
            "createdAt": "2026-10-09T05:55:58Z",
            "databaseId": 6075218848,
            "updatedAt": "2026-10-09T05:55:58Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/60667#issuecomment-6075218848"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
