            },
            "body": "> Without an out-of-place copy, this causes an all-zero-accuracy issue under torch.compile — see #39844.\r\n> \r\n> If we really want to use inplace allreduce, we may need to rely on an environment variable or some other mechanism to determine whether inplace is actually safe to use here. torch.compiler.is_compiling() doesn't work when use custom op all_reduce.\r\n\r\nyou're right. we should check eager mode here. but at this point, compilation_config is not available and a WA is to check is_breakable_cudagraph_enabled.",
