  "issue_comments": [
    {
      "body": "cc @yma11 @rogerxfeng8  @chaojun-zhang  please evaluate ",
      "created_at": "2026-10-09T01:16:51Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/60667#issuecomment-6072267644",
      "id": 6072267644,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-09T01:16:51Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "jikunshang"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "@xinyu-intel Can you explain more about `torch.compile should already handle this`? Previous change is decided mainly to keep same handle process vs cuda path and avoid accuracy issue in some corner cases, I remember also related with `torch.compile`? ",
      "created_at": "2026-10-09T04:56:37Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/60667#issuecomment-6074563750",
      "id": 6074563750,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-09T04:56:37Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "yma11"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Without an out-of-place copy, this causes an all-zero-accuracy issue under torch.compile — see https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/39844.\r\n\r\nIf we really want to use inplace allreduce, we may need to rely on an environment variable or some other mechanism to determine whether inplace is actually safe to use here. torch.compiler.is_compiling() doesn't work when use custom op all_reduce.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-09T05:55:58Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/60667#issuecomment-6075218848",
      "id": 6075218848,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-09T05:55:58Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "chaojun-zhang"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "> Without an out-of-place copy, this causes an all-zero-accuracy issue under torch.compile — see #39844.\r\n> \r\n> If we really want to use inplace allreduce, we may need to rely on an environment variable or some other mechanism to determine whether inplace is actually safe to use here. torch.compiler.is_compiling() doesn't work when use custom op all_reduce.\r\n\r\nyou're right. we should check eager mode here. but at this point, compilation_config is not available and a WA is to check is_breakable_cudagraph_enabled.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-09T06:29:55Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/60667#issuecomment-6075662968",
      "id": 6075662968,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-09T06:29:55Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "xinyu-intel"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Minor: PR title starts with [XPU].",
      "created_at": "2026-10-09T06:39:13Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/60667#issuecomment-6075781676",
